    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Approach**\n\nI'm focusing on defining the approach. My current plan is to build a Python script, `timestamped_transcript.py`, that extracts and returns timestamps from a transcription result. I need to make a solid choice on an external speech-to-text provider, and ensure it's clearly identifiable within the code for easy future modification, since it will be a key component.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Speech-to-Text. I'm building `timestamped_transcript.py`, which will feature a function, `get_word_timestamps`, that parses Google's JSON response format. This function takes the transcription result and returns a list of dictionaries with word, start time, and end time. I'll include the Google Cloud import. I'm focusing on the logic to extract data from the response.\n\n\n**Structuring the Extraction**\n\nI'm structuring the code now. I'm building `timestamped_transcript.py` with a function, `get_word_timestamps`, to extract the word timestamps, assuming a Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API response as input (JSON format). I'm focusing on parsing the `results`, `alternatives`, and `words` array to get the `startTime`, `endTime`, and `word`. The goal is a function returning a list of dictionaries. I included the import for `google.cloud.speech_v1p1beta1`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820600355,
          "start": 1789820597336
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99ef458001Pf8htIbRCxmJaw",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99eef60001k6s4ZceXPerLyi",
      "session_id": "ses_f466110b8ffeTuDzJ9LrfGv4z2",
      "time_created": 1789820597337,
      "time_updated": 1789820600355
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "2OunGIOvUjrlZh8t",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import speech_v1p1beta1 as speech\n\ndef get_word_timestamps(transcription_result):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts word-level timestamps from a Google Cloud Speech-to-Text transcription result.\n\n    Args:\n        transcription_result (dict): The JSON response from Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A list of dictionaries, where each dictionary contains 'word',\n              'start_time' (in seconds), and 'end_time' (in seconds).\n    \"\"\"\n    timestamps = []\n    if \"results\" in transcription_result:\n        for result in transcription_result[\"results\"]:\n            if \"alternatives\" in result:\n                for alternative in result[\"alternatives\"]:\n                    if \"words\" in alternative:\n                        for word_info in alternative[\"words\"]:\n                            start_seconds = int(word_info[\"startTime\"][:-1]) if \"startTime\" in word_info and word_info[\"startTime\"] else 0\n                            end_seconds = int(word_info[\"endTime\"][:-1]) if \"endTime\" in word_info and word_info[\"endTime\"] else 0\n                            timestamps.append({\n                                \"word\": word_info.get(\"word\"),\n                                \"start_time\": start_seconds,\n                                \"end_time\": end_seconds,\n                            })\n    return timestamps\n",
            "filePath": "timestamped_transcript.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
