      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Speech-to-Text. I need to figure out how to integrate it as the identifiable external provider within the `poll_transcription.py `file.\n\n\n**Implementing the Polling Function**\n\nI'm now focused on the specifics of implementing the `poll_transcription_job` function within `poll_transcription.py`. I'll initialize the Google Cloud Speech client and use the `long_running_recognize().result()` method to handle the asynchronous nature of the transcription process. My plan is to extract the relevant transcript from the response, specifically navigating the `results` and `alternatives` fields to retrieve the text.\n\n\n**Defining the Structure**\n\nNow I'm focusing on structuring the `poll_transcription.py` file itself. I've settled on the `google-cloud-speech` library, assuming it's pre-installed. I'll include the relevant import. The core of my approach is implementing the `poll_transcription_job` function, accepting an `operation_name` and using `SpeechClient` to poll the long-running operation. My priority is extracting and returning the transcript, referencing `results` and then `alternatives` from the operation's response.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820591084,
          "start": 1789820588306
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99ed112001TlSHVtan9v0hCV",
